.TH RECORD 1 "2026-09-14" "record 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
record \- retain and replay an observed Unix process boundary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B record run -f SESSION
[flags] -- COMMAND [ARG ...]
.br
.B record replay -f SESSION
[-stream NAME | -json]
.br
.B record check -f SESSION
.br
.B record help
.br
.B record version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run records one literal invocation as sealed Ask notes in a new session.
Replay verifies the complete snapshot before emitting retained stdout and
stderr. It never executes the recorded command or contacts its services.
Ask 0.3 or later is required. Filesystem and network effects outside selected
observations are not implied by a process receipt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -f FILE
Explicit session. Run refuses an existing destination.
.TP
.B -ask COMMAND
Ask executable, default ask.
.TP
.B -input FILE
Snapshot a regular file before execution. Repeatable.
.TP
.B -output FILE
Snapshot a regular file after execution. Repeatable.
.TP
.B -session FILE
Retain and verify a child Ask session after execution. Repeatable.
.TP
.B -pass-fd N
Pass a private inherited descriptor without reading it. Repeatable.
.TP
.B -label TEXT
Explicit non-secret context. Repeatable.
.TP
.B -timeout D
Optional execution limit, such as 30s. Default unlimited.
.TP
.B -stream NAME
Replay extracts stdin, stdout, stderr, or artifact:N to stdout.
.TP
.B -json
Replay emits the verified invocation and terminal receipt as JSON.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Run and replay preserve the child status. Signals use 128 plus signal.
Recorder errors and incomplete evidence return 125. Extraction, JSON, and
check return 0 after verification. Completion of capture is not business
success or resolution of uncertain external effects.
.SH SECURITY
Environment values and private descriptor contents are not captured.
Credentials explicitly placed in argv, streams, labels, or snapshots will
be recorded. Use private descriptor handoffs instead. A recording is a
self-contained sensitive file. Seals are integrity commitments, not signatures.
.SH SEE ALSO
ask(1), trail(1)

.TP
.BI -grace " duration"
After forwarding an interrupt, terminate the child process group after this
grace period (default 1s), even if its leader exits first. A supervisor should
allow a longer cleanup period for Record itself. Normal exits do not kill
intentionally detached work.
